NAME
    source, . - execute commands from a file in the current shell

SYNOPSIS
    source <path>
    . <path>

DESCRIPTION
    Reads <path> inside the shell sandbox and executes its lines in the
    current shell's variable scope. Assignments made by the script remain
    visible after source returns (unlike $(...) command substitution,
    which runs in an isolated subshell).

    Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is '#' are
    skipped. Multi-line control-flow blocks (if, for, while, until) may
    span lines in the file. Script lines are not added to command history
    and do not perform '!' history expansion; only the source invocation
    itself is recorded.

    Nesting is capped at 20 levels to prevent recursive script loops. An
    unterminated block at end of file prints an error and clears pending
    input.

EXAMPLES
    source /Logs/setup.sh
    . setup.sh

EXIT STATUS
    0   Script ran to completion (or stopped on a host request).
    1   Missing path, path outside sandbox, file not found, read error,
        or nesting depth exceeded.

SEE ALSO
    export(1), history(1), trust(1), dianash(1)
